1068
02:22:10,855 --> 02:22:15,335
But self-discipline is about more than just training and competition.

1069
02:22:15,335 --> 02:22:20,275
In fact, many of the most disciplined individuals are just regular people who have gradually

1070
02:22:20,275 --> 02:22:24,275
developed enough self-control to accomplish their goals.

1071
02:22:24,275 --> 02:22:28,915
Whether you want to start your own company, lose weight, or just stop watching so much

1072
02:22:28,915 --> 02:22:34,956
TV, self-discipline is an incredibly useful skill that keeps you motivated, clear-headed,

1073
02:22:34,956 --> 02:22:37,395
and focused on your objective.

1074
02:22:37,395 --> 02:22:41,175
But what exactly is the secret to building self-discipline?

1075
02:22:41,175 --> 02:22:45,675
Despite what you might have seen in movies, you don't have to meditate on a mountaintop

1076
02:22:45,675 --> 02:22:48,855
or wax an old man's car a dozen times.

1077
02:22:48,855 --> 02:22:54,735
These kinds of extremes, while entertaining, don't actually work because time and consistency

1078
02:22:54,735 --> 02:22:59,215
are essential for anyone hoping to live a more disciplined life.

1079
02:22:59,215 --> 02:23:03,915
So the real key to developing self-discipline is moderation.

1080
02:23:03,915 --> 02:23:08,175
Doing something in moderation means having the power to stop yourself when you've had

1081
02:23:08,175 --> 02:23:09,375
enough.

1082
02:23:09,375 --> 02:23:13,995
If you want to have a more controlled diet or reduce the time you spend playing video

1083
02:23:13,995 --> 02:23:18,875
games, you shouldn't try to suddenly make extreme changes to your lifestyle.

1084
02:23:18,875 --> 02:23:25,036
Instead, focus on moderating your behavior, reducing your bad habits little by little to

1085
02:23:25,036 --> 02:23:29,495
develop the kind of self-discipline that will last a lifetime.

1086
02:23:29,495 --> 02:23:32,335
So how do you put all of this into practice?

1087
02:23:32,335 --> 02:23:37,255
Here are 7 strategies you can use to master self-discipline.

1088
02:23:37,255 --> 02:23:38,635
Number 1.

1089
02:23:38,635 --> 02:23:40,635
Find your weaknesses.

1090
02:23:40,635 --> 02:23:45,855
No matter what kind of bad habits you have, the first and most important step toward becoming

1091
02:23:45,855 --> 02:23:50,835
a more disciplined person is identifying and accepting your weaknesses.

1092
02:23:50,835 --> 02:23:55,375
The simple truth is that everyone in the world has a weakness for something, whether it's

1093
02:23:55,375 --> 02:24:00,635
eating junk food, drinking too much coffee, or spending money you don't have.

1094
02:24:00,635 --> 02:24:05,415
While some weaknesses are more destructive than others, building self-discipline isn't

1095
02:24:05,415 --> 02:24:10,175
about getting rid of those weaknesses, but learning how to control them.

1096
02:24:10,175 --> 02:24:17,255
Many people never even get to this stage because they can't accept how little control they have over their own actions.

1097
02:24:17,255 --> 02:24:21,835
This kind of denial can lead to addiction, so it's important that you address these issues

1098
02:24:21,835 --> 02:24:24,575
before they take over your life.

1099
02:24:24,575 --> 02:24:29,515
For many people, the idea of moderation is much less intimidating than cutting yourself

1100
02:24:29,515 --> 02:24:30,935
off completely.

1101
02:24:30,935 --> 02:24:35,795
So instead of focusing about which bad habits you need to remove, think about which ones

1102
02:24:35,795 --> 02:24:37,795
you'd like to lessen.

1103
02:24:37,795 --> 02:24:39,295
Number 2.

1104
02:24:39,295 --> 02:24:41,435
Create Easy Habits.

1105
02:24:41,435 --> 02:24:46,135
On your road to becoming a more disciplined person, you're going to develop a set of new

1106
02:24:46,135 --> 02:24:50,735
and improved habits, but it isn't going to happen overnight.

1107
02:24:50,735 --> 02:24:53,075
Imagine you're trying to lose 20 pounds.

1108
02:24:53,075 --> 02:24:57,655
You can't just wake up one morning and decide it's time for a 30 minute run when you haven't

1109
02:24:57,655 --> 02:24:59,655
worked out in years.

1110
02:24:59,655 --> 02:25:05,275
You're going to end up exhausted, sore, and unmotivated, so you should start slow and work

1111
02:25:05,275 --> 02:25:08,395
up towards your goal over time.

1112
02:25:08,395 --> 02:25:14,755
Plan out more manageable, easier workouts that leave you feeling optimistic and proud of yourself.

1113
02:25:14,755 --> 02:25:19,255
Remember that the goal isn't to lose all the weight in one day, but to create healthier

1114
02:25:19,255 --> 02:25:25,335
habits that you genuinely enjoy doing, even after you've reached your ultimate goal.

1115
02:25:25,335 --> 02:25:26,555
Number 3.

1116
02:25:26,555 --> 02:25:28,675
Use Rewards.

1117
02:25:28,675 --> 02:25:33,395
Positive reinforcement is a great way to make sure that your new habits stick around, so

1118
02:25:33,395 --> 02:25:36,715
don't be afraid to reward yourself for improving.

1119
02:25:36,715 --> 02:25:41,595
In the same way that you give a dog a treat when they sit, people are more likely to behave

1120
02:25:41,595 --> 02:25:45,595
a certain way when they know there's a reward on the line.

1121
02:25:45,595 --> 02:25:48,595
The goal is to make sure that your new habits are not going to be able to be able to be able

1122
02:25:48,595 --> 02:25:49,595
to be able to be able to be able to be able to be able to be able to be able to be able to

1123
02:25:49,595 --> 02:25:50,595
be able to be able to be able to be able to be able to be able to be able to be able to be able

1124
02:25:45,396 --> 02:25:51,216
Rewards will also motivate them to work harder by giving them something positive to look forward to.

1125
02:25:51,695 --> 02:25:56,976
This is especially useful for people who are having a hard time getting their new habits started

1126
02:25:56,976 --> 02:26:01,836
because they haven't developed enough self-discipline to push through the beginning stages.

1127
02:26:02,355 --> 02:26:07,156
Say you want to cut out sugary foods from your diet but are struggling to keep it up.

1128
02:26:07,456 --> 02:26:12,896
By using a reward system, you can focus all of your attention on the cookie or brownie

1129
02:26:12,896 --> 02:26:18,096
that's waiting for you at the end of the day, making it easier to avoid breaking your diet otherwise.

1130
02:26:18,996 --> 02:26:25,056
This way, you are always in control of your habits and impulses instead of letting them control you.

1131
02:26:25,716 --> 02:26:28,096
4. Personal Standards

1132
02:26:28,096 --> 02:26:36,016
Disciplined people often motivate themselves to keep pushing by strictly adhering to a set of standards for their own life.

1133
02:26:36,355 --> 02:26:42,855
Standards are basically personal limits, which lay out the absolute minimum that you're willing to accept for yourself.

1134
02:26:42,896 --> 02:26:49,396
But these kinds of boundaries only work if you are willing to hold yourself accountable when you break them.

1135
02:26:49,855 --> 02:26:56,976
This is where most people struggle because they end up setting really high standards that are impossible to meet consistently.

1136
02:26:57,476 --> 02:27:01,855
It's important to remember that standards and goals are not the same thing.

1137
02:27:02,336 --> 02:27:09,695
While goals are things you work and reach for over time, you should realistically be able to meet your standards every single day.

1138
02:27:09,695 --> 02:27:16,855
Writers, for example, might aim to write 3,000 words a day, but have a standard of only 2,000.

1139
02:27:17,576 --> 02:27:19,876
Why are personal standards so useful?

1140
02:27:20,516 --> 02:27:23,936
Most people tend to have an all-or-nothing approach to their goals.

1141
02:27:24,296 --> 02:27:27,456
Either they can get it done immediately or just give up.

1142
02:27:28,036 --> 02:27:35,376
So, by setting standards, you give yourself a reason to keep working even when you aren't actually able to achieve your goal.

1143
02:27:35,376 --> 02:27:38,076
Number 5. Look ahead

1144
02:27:38,076 --> 02:27:45,876
After you've identified what your weaknesses are, it's important that you realize when you're putting yourself in dangerous situations.

1145
02:27:46,656 --> 02:27:50,076
Imagine you're trying to limit how much fast food you eat.

1146
02:27:50,436 --> 02:27:56,195
You used to eat a burger and fries for lunch every day, but have decided to switch over to salads.

1147
02:27:56,736 --> 02:28:00,736
So, would it be a good idea to eat your salad inside a McDonald's?

1148
02:28:00,736 --> 02:28:07,396
My point is that you should recognize situations where your weaknesses might get the best of you and avoid them.

1149
02:28:07,736 --> 02:28:14,376
If you want to stop getting distracted by your phone at work, for example, turn it onto airplane mode at the beginning of the day

1150
02:28:14,376 --> 02:28:19,416
or leave your phone in your bag to make sure you couldn't get distracted even if you wanted to.

1151
02:28:19,936 --> 02:28:27,756
Of course, there are certain times when it's impossible to avoid your weaknesses, so make it easier on yourself by planning ahead.

1152
02:28:27,756 --> 02:28:36,115
Figure out what you're going to do to avoid falling back into old habits and find a way to reward yourself for resisting the temptation.

1153
02:28:36,756 --> 02:28:42,876
This kind of planning not only helps you stay on track, but also gives you a sense of control over your life.

1154
02:28:43,615 --> 02:28:45,676
Number 6. Set alarms

1155
02:28:45,676 --> 02:28:49,695
Time is a slippery slope when it comes to bad habits.

1156
02:28:49,695 --> 02:28:55,956
If you tend to watch too much TV, play too many video games, or waste hours on social media,

1157
02:28:56,355 --> 02:29:03,296
you know how easy it is to justify spending a few more minutes to complete a mission or watch the rest of an episode.

1158
02:29:03,936 --> 02:29:10,756
But, a few minutes can easily turn into a few hours, and before you know it, you've used up the whole night.

1159
02:29:11,436 --> 02:29:15,576
So, how can you use moderation to make sure this doesn't keep happening?

1160
02:29:15,576 --> 02:29:23,876
Most people tend to focus on removing the TV and video games, getting rid of them even though they weren't the problem in the first place.

1161
02:29:24,376 --> 02:29:27,436
The real problem is how much time you spend on them.

1162
02:29:28,036 --> 02:29:33,876
In other words, you can keep playing the games you love as long as you stay within a set time limit.

1163
02:29:34,436 --> 02:29:40,855
Next time you start up any game, set an alarm for one hour, and make sure you turn the volume all the way up.

1164
